on  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 CAM REMOVED_DATE are positive in isolated single tumor cells  These cells are only seen on the immunohistochemical stained slide and cannot be definitively identified on the H E sections  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary sentinel node   is a tan yellow fatty portion of soft tissue containing three lymph nodes  One lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining two whole nodes are submitted in toto as FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm left breast simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm portion of grossly unremarkable white skin on one surface  There is a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm wrinkled tan nipple and areolar complex with a 2 0cm grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen is oriented with a suture designating 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm indurated  ill defined gray pink mass which is located in the central  subareolar region of the specimen  The mass extends to within 4 0cm of the posterior resection margin  1 5cm of the skin surface  There is an abundant amount of slightly granular gray white fibrous tissue surrounding the mass  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a scant amount interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  lymph nodes are not grossly identified  Representative sections 