  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  There is a short stitch denoting the superior aspect  a long stitch denoting the lateral aspect  and short and long stitches denoting the deep margin  The entire specimen is inked black  the deep margin is overinked in blue  and the lateral margin is overinked in red  Sectioning reveals a 1cm in greatest dimension somewhat stellate and granular tan lesion abutting the anteriolateral margin approximately 3 0cm inferior to the superior margin  Additionally there is a 1 0cm in greatest dimension tan pink slightly firm nodule  located more inferiorly  which comes within 0 3cm of the lateral margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular  slightly gritty white lesion which is located even more inferiorly and abuts the lateral margin grossly  Section code  A  FX 1  representative section of stellate lesion  B C  Remainder of stellate lesion  relative to anterolateral margin  D  Nodule relative to lateral margin  E F  Irregular white  gritty lesion  entirely submitted  relative to lateral margin  G  FX 2  tissue from inferior pole  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular fragment of fibroadipose tissue  consisting of grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is entirely submitted in H L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional shaved margin  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of multiple pieces of fibroadipose tissue  No gross lesions are identified  The entire specimen is submitted in M R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  with a short suture on the superior margin  and a long suture on the lateral margin  The entire specimen is inked in black  and the superior aspect is overinked in blue  No gross lesions are identified within the parenchyma  and the specimen is submitted from lateral to medial in S V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  R axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm irregular fragment of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue  Lymph nodes from this specimen are submitted in W BB  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  ABUTTING INK AT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SHORT SUTURE  NO DEFINITIVE INVASION SEEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE SAMPLED BY SURGEON WITH REQUEST FOR FROZEN   FIBROUS BREAST TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Jaime A Rivera  M D  Simon Kaspar Ashiku  M D  Hasan Bazari  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL NODE DISSECTI PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGIN    NCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISIO PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCIS PART E  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISION   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 53 CLINICAL DATA  Excisional biopsy of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS WITH FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  MIXED LOW AND INTERMEDIATE GRADE  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 22 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular 2 5cm firm tan white mass  which is 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and frozen section  2  The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes A through G  Frozen section  1 submitted as H  and frozen section  2 is submitted in cassette I  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , No.
