n 0 5cm of the posterior margin  to within 1 0cm of the anterior margin  to within 1 0cm of the inferior margin  and 0 3cm of the medial margin  and 0 3cm of the lateral margin  Also identified is a metallic clip  The tissue surrounding the cavity is tan yellow and fatty  No other masses or lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body of specimen submitted sequentially from medial to lateral  with the section containing the clip in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral resection margin en face  Final Diagnosis by Joshua Kish M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Some ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain   1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Not_reported.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Veronica Klepeis  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  Invasive ductal carcinoma  right breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH MATRIX PRODUCTION  SEE TABLE  1 2  PROLIFERATION OF SMALL TUBULES  CONSISTENT WITH ATYPICAL MICROGLANDULAR ADENOSIS 3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  glass slide measurement  GRADE  3 LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NOTE  The adenosis consists of infiltrative tubules of atypical epithelial cells which contain enlarged pleomorphic nuclei with some prominent nucleoli  Some of the epithelial cells are apoptotic  In addition  there are scattered intraluminal eosinophilic secretions  Focally  some tubules appear to be lined by myoepithelial cells as evidenced by faint staining for calponin  p63  and heavy chain myosin  The epithelial cells within these tubules are strongly positive for S 100 and cytokeratin  and negative for estrogen receptor and epithelial membrane antigen  These features support the diagnosis of atypical microglandular adenosis  This atypical microglandular adenosis extends at least 1 9cm beyond the mass of high grade carcinoma  and is present at the inferior  superior  posterior  and anterior margins of the specimen  Dr  F  Koerner has reviewed selected slides and concurs with the diagnosis of atypical microglandular adenosis  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  ATYPICAL MICROGLANDULAR ADENOSIS  PRESENT AT THE TRUE TISSUE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  heavy chain myosin  p63  and calponin highlight the presence of myoepithelial cells  The lobular carcinoma cells are negative for e cadherin  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  ATYPICAL MICROGLANDULAR ADENOSIS  PRESENT AT THE TRUE TISSUE MARGIN BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MYXOID FIBROADENOMA  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL     REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink to yellow nodular tissue consisting of a lymph node with attached adipose tissue  The surrounding fat is removed and the lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a 