Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA   100   GRADE I III  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM CLOSEST INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  2  FIBROADENOMA  1 5 MM   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  4  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan  breast biopsy with a hard  smooth nodule palpated beneath the adipose tissue  This specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  gray  poorly circumscribed lesion REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  abutting an inked resection margin  Submitted entirely in A through C  with lesion in A and B  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No.
