g of the invasive and in situ components may not be entirely accurate  There is striking fibrosis within the tumor which is likely secondary to chemotherapy effect  The lymph nodes show marked therapy related fibrosis as well  The metastatic tumor within the lymph nodes consists of aggregates of tumor   0 2cm  and single cells scattered throughout the fibrotic stroma  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains help confirm the presence of tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  No definite extracapsular extension is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN FOUR OUT OF FOUR LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lymph nodes show significant fibrosis  consistent with chemotherapy effect  Cytokeratin immunoperoxidase stains confirm the presence of scattered tumor cells within the more fibrotic lymph nodes  There is tumor present within extranodal lymphatic vessels  but no definite extracapsular extension is identified  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right modified radical mastectomy  is a an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is surfaced by an REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan pink areola  The areola comes to 1 8cm of the superior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unremarkable tan pink nipple which comes to 2 2cm of the closest inferior margin  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a fairly well defined  largely centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm indurated tan pink mass with several contiguous peripheral nodules predominantly along the inferior and medial aspects o