Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 28 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SEVERAL NODULES  THE LARGEST SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone 