ion  0 2cm from the posterior margin  and 0 5cm from the anterior margin  In addition  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan fibrous area  just superior to the nipple where a metal clip is identified  This area is 0 9cm from the anterior margin and 3 7cm from the posterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and lobulated to focally tan and fibrous  An intraparenchymal lymph node is identified in the lower outer quadrant breast tissue  The axillary region is dissected for lymph nodes and several candidate lymph nodes are grossly identified  There is one candidate lymph node that grossly abuts the axillary mass  Sections are submitted as follows  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  submitted from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Axillary mass to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area with metal clip to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant breast parenchyma to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin from lateral portion of skin ellipse   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two additional candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Single large lymph node in axillary region which appears to abut the axillary mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intraparenchymal lymph node  bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm aggregate of yellow lobulated soft tissue that is disse