rmone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm red and yellow breast tissue fragment with a localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 4cm tan  firm  rubbery to gritty central region with faintly retracted borders  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through I  with the tan central region in A through D  Gross Description by  Douglas B  Flieder  MD Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES AND A MINUTE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR    0 4CM   TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
