Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 41 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  FORMING MANY NODULES WITHIN A REGION SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 7 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus in one lymph node consists of just a few cells  The malignant cells do not transgress the lymph node capsules  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 98 at 15 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a left mastectomy specimen  27 x 14 x 2cm  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed  grossly unremarkable nipple  and a 4 x 0 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed 3cm well healed scar  4cm inferolateral to the first skin ellipse  An ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm firm  white healing biopsy cavity with surrounding punctate areas of fat necrosis is present immediately inferior to the skin ellipse containing the well healed scar  The ill defined  firm area comes to within 0 1cm of the closest deep inked resection margin  0 1cm of the closest anterior resection margin  9cm from the superior resection margin and 3 5cm from the closest inferior resection margin  More firm nodular areas spanning 4 0cm are present surrounding the biopsy cavity  which come to within 0 2cm of the closest inked deep resection margin and within 0 1cm of the closest anterior inked resection margin  More gritty areas surrounding the biopsy cavity in the areas of fat necrosis are present  grossly coming to within 0 5cm of the closest anterior inked resection margin  Within the axillary tissue  several lymph nodes ranging from 0 4cm to 2cm in greatest dimension are identified  the largest grossly suspicious for involvement by tumor  SECTION CODE A B  Biopsy cavity  including closest deep inked resection margin  C F  Representative sections of more firm nodular areas  in relation to deep inked resection margin  G J  Representative sections of more gritty areas adjacent to areas of fat necrosis in relation to the closest anterior inked resection margin  K  Representative section of breast parenchyma away from tumor  L N  Nodes from axillary tail  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  Saha Sadeghi  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENSIVELY PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and vascular invasion are not identified  Estrogen and progesterone receptors are ordered  Diagnosis by  Deborah S  Fleischhacker  MD ScD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm oval portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reval a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm area near one end which consists of dense fibrous tissue extending to the inked margin  Entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A B  Fibrous area  C F  Remainder  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  FOCALLY FIRM PARENCHYMA  BUT NO DISCRETE MASS IDENTIFIED  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
