Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 96 at 11 46 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADMIXED WITH AND ADJACENT TO INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Invasive tumor extends to within 0 2cm of the nearest  superior  margin  Definite blood vascular invasion is not identified  BREAST  RIGHT SUPERIOR MARGIN   FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  22 MAY 96 at 15 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 96 at 09 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Designated  right breast  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast fragment  inked black  with anterior superior surface overinked blue and anterior inferior surface overinked green  Sectioned to show an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm stellate  firm  white mass within 0 3cm of the superior surface  Representative sections submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes A K  with entire mass included  Designated  superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast fragment containing a short suture designating the superior aspect  The long suture  to designate the posterior deep margin  has been previously separated from the specimen  One surface of the breast fragment is flat  and the other is curved with lobulated fat  The curved surface is overinked blue in the superior region and green in the inferior region  The parenchyma is unremarkable  and representative sections are submitted from one end to the other in L T  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  William E Butler  M D  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST PART B  SUPERIOR MARGIN   report_end  , No.
