Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  11 AUG 97 at 18 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 44 OF 45 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Carcinoma extends beyond the lymph node capsule in numerous lymph nodes  LYMPH NODES   HIGHEST RIGHT AXILLA    METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 AUG 97 at 14 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  right breast and axillary contents  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  which is covered by REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm ellipse of unremarkable skin with unremarkable nipple with no apparent scars  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 3 7cm lobulated white tan  focally necrotic tumor 2 0cm from the posterior margin  A section of tumor with the closest margin is submitted in A  Additional samples of tumor are submitted in B D  Samples of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in E F  A sample of unremarkable skeletal muscle measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm is submitted in G  Lymph nodes are submitted in H P  Labeled  highest axillary node  is a piece of fatty tissue with a lymph node measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  submitted entirely in Q  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  HIGHEST RIGHT AXILLARY   EXCISION   report_end  , Not_reported.
