Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 31 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  1    LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  2   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  1  In areas the tumor has a tubular pattern  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the inked superior resection margin  The tumor is 0 9cm in greatest dimension no lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  The single focus of LCIS  slide M  is 0 3cm from a superior margin  NOTE  2  The focus of lobular carcinoma in situ is within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 20 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in three separately labeled parts  Labeled  left  breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with 2 attached sutures  a long one designating the lateral aspect and a short one designating the superior aspect  The superior portion is inked green  Sectioning reveals firm  white tan  focally  red and gritty  irregular breast parenchyma extending to the inked margins  A representative section of the firm area 1 5cm from lateral edge is frozen as FX 1  Another firm area  1cm in diameterm  0 1cm from the inked margin  lies adjacent to the short suture is frozen as FX 2  The FX 2 is sent to Cox 5  SECTION CODE  A M  entire breast parenchyma  from superior portion to inferior portion  N  FX 1  lateral margin  Labeled  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tan  focally yellow  focally cystic  irregular  cut surfaces  submitted entirely in O through S  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing several lymph nodes  ranging in largest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  The larger ones have whitish tan solid cut surface  Representative half of each lymph node is submitted in T and U  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT LATERAL  BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA    TUBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  2 SPECIMENS  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 07 CLINICAL DATA  IOG                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SEVERAL NODULES  TOGETHER ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN AND TO REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  NEEDLE ASPIRATION TRACK  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGINS    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 54     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm vertical skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior  deep  is inked black  lateral is green  medial is blue  and anterior is yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined nodule which is 0 3cm from the closest deep and anterior margins  and away from other margins  There are few satellite nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm at the superior side of the main mass but away from the margins  No Frozen Section is done  Section code  A  superior margin B E  satellite nodules F G  mass close to anterior margin H I  mass close to posterior margin J  inferior mar