Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Kristina Braaten  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Re excision right breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID PAPILLARY TYPE  PRESENT IN 2 OF 6 BLOCKS  AND PRESENT  0 05 CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN TWO FOCI ON OPPOSITE SIDES OF A TISSUE SECTION  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for myoepithelial markers  p63  calponin  and myosin  show rare cells at the periphery of the tumor nodules  which are conservatively interpreted as representing a markedly attenuated myoepithelial cell layer and therefore supporting an interpretation of DCIS  However  stomal invasion cannot be entirely excluded  Individually  the foci of residual tumor are small  about 0 3cm  however  they span 2 2cm of tissue  BREAST  RIGHT  SHAVED MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  TEHRE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  SHAVED CEPHALAD MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are three containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  re excision right breast cancer   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm unoriented portion of tan yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue  inked black and serially sectioned to reveal diffuse tan yellow foci of fat necrosis  some of which are present at the inked margin  Two metallic clips are identified in one of the cross sections  No discrete masses or lesions are noted  Represe