Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 50 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3   ABUTTING SEVERAL INKED RESECTION MARGINS   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40    WITH FOCAL HIGH GRADE NUCLEI  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INFILTRATING COMPONENT AND PRESENTS AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic carcinoma is noted  An area of ductal carcinoma in situ displays a focus of high grade cells and this focus is less than 0 05cm  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas 