 we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five parts  Received in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and accompanying X ray film  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal scattered cystic structure ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through J  with area corresponding to calcification in cassettes A through D  Received in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch designating the superior margin and the long stitch designating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked entirely with black and additionally with yellow posteriorly  deep margin   and superiorly wi