formance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast with a short stitch indicating superior and a long stitch indicating lateral  Three needle localization wires are identified adjacent to the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  medial in red  lateral in yellow  anterior in blue  posterior in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular firm area with multiple calcifications  which comes to 0 5cm from the closest posterior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm well demarcated  tan yellow area with calcifications  which abuts the anterior  posterior  and lateral  and medial margins  Also identified is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregularly shaped  firm  tan yellow nodule which abuts the lateral margin and is 0 4cm from the closest posterior margin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A K  calcified firm area is in B C  the 0 6cm nodule in D  and the 3 0cm area in E K   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast with a short stitch designating the superior margin  a long stitch designating the lateral margin and a double stitch designating the edge furthest from tumor  The external surface shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular shaped  tan white firm mass on the lateral side  The specimen is inked as follows  medial in red  lateral in yellow  anterior in blue  posterior  with double stitch  in black  Sectioning the specimen from medial to lateral reveals the tan white firm area appreciated from the external surface  which abuts all margins  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette L S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan green lymph node with attached fibroadipose tissue  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette T  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL    report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA  Known breast cancer reviewed at Brigham and Women s Hospital  invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Scattered tumor cells   25  are detected on cytokeratin immunostains only  a total of 3 stains examined   The involved lymph node measures 1 3cm  and extranodal involvement is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE AND IN SITU MAMMARY CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma is predominately lobular in its morphology  but there are focal areas of cohesion and polarization  An E cadherin stain demonstrates predominately only cytoplasmic staining of these in situ tumor cells  but in the focal cohesive areas  membranous staining is noted  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain shows strong cytoplasmic staining  Together  these morphologic and immunohistochemical findings are consistent with an in situ carcinoma with both lobular and ductal features  As the invasive component is morphologically similar to the in situ component  it is also classified as having features of both lobular and ductal carcinoma  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Main 2 5cm mass and multiple satellite nodules  aggregating to at least 3cm in total  Tumor extends into the dermis  Grade  2  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Grade of in situ carcinoma  3  Location of in situ carcinoma  Within and beyond